      "writtenOn": "2024-05-20T17:21:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given the two comments above, I wondering what the value is in have the client pass in an optional Recorder. In an ideal world those Recorders would be on different threads and thus not safe to use here. It also starts intermixing what we decided was meant to be a \"non repeatable\" (i.e. not on a recording) with possible recorded work by the client. So it really seems like if a client wanted to pass in a Recorder here, it should be a dedicated Recorder for these asyncReadBack calls only. If that is the case, then does it not just make sense for us to handle all this ourselves under the hood? Either by making a new Recoder each time or letting the Context own a helper Recoder it keeps alive throughout its life time.\n\nNow after saying all that, if what I suggest above is valid, does it really matter if the textures from the async reads are part of the scratch system since they\u0027ll most likely be on internal Recorders/Recordings that don\u0027t even have other draws to share textures with?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 245,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 95
      },
